# Coding quality

## Comments

- **No comments** in application code. Names, types, and structure must carry meaning.
- **Exception:** Solidity / smart contracts — use **NatSpec** (`@title`, `@notice`, `@param`, `@return`, `@dev` only when non-obvious).
- Never narrate (`// increment i`, `// call MoMo`). Never leave TODOs that mask unfinished design.
- Prefer deleting dead code over commenting it out.

## Efficiency

- Do the smallest change that solves the task — no speculative abstractions.
- No unused imports, variables, exports, or dependencies.
- Avoid N+1 queries, unbounded loops over network I/O, and sync work on hot paths.
- Hot paths (invoice accept → disburse): minimize allocations; prefer streaming/subscribe over poll storms.
- Integer money only (`msat`, RWF). Never `number` floats for value.

## Consistency

- Match existing naming, file layout, and patterns in the touched package.
- One style per concern: errors, logging, validation, HTTP handlers.
- Public APIs: stable names from `docs/OFFRAMP_FLOW.md` / `packages/shared`.

## Structure

- Functions do one thing; early return over deep nesting.
- Pure domain logic free of HTTP/gRPC/MoMo clients — inject ports at edges.
- No god files; split by feature when a module exceeds clear responsibility.

## Forbidden

```ts
// ❌ BAD
// Settle the invoice after MoMo succeeds
await settle(preimage);

// ✅ GOOD
await settle(preimage);
```
